{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3138","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3138","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3138\",\"parent_revision\":\"e5fc6593af21e7701d3cc850bec544e02377071437f940b20b165c16a16bc2dc\",\"root_revision\":\"e5fc6593af21e7701d3cc850bec544e02377071437f940b20b165c16a16bc2dc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEvery agent definition that uses MCP tools enumerates them by exact name in its `tools:` frontmatter. This couples the MCP server's tool code to agent frontmatter bidirectionally, with no enforcement and silent failure in both directions.\\n\\nRemoving or renaming a tool on the server leaves dead entries in every agent that listed it. Adding a tool to the server means no agent can see it until every relevant `tools:` list is edited by hand. Neither direction produces an error \u2014 the agent simply runs without the tool it was written to depend on.\\n\\nMeasured on 2026-08-22 (four probe agents, definitions registered before spawning): a nonexistent MCP tool name in a `tools:` list is dropped silently while the rest of the grant survives, so a stale entry is invisible. `tools: *` grants the full set. A server-scoped wildcard such as `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*` fails open \u2014 it grants everything rather than scoping to that server \u2014 so it is not a usable workaround and is actively dangerous.\\n\\nImpact: two concrete instances of this drift already exist in the repository. `artifact_migrate` appears in 14 agent files and does not exist on the backlog server. Eleven MCP servers are referenced across agent definitions and are not connected in this project, including one agent written to depend on a crawler it can never receive.\\n\\nPayoff: a check that compares every `tools:` entry across `plugins/**/agents/*.md` against the servers' advertised tools, and fails loudly, converts a silent capability loss into a build failure. It would also subsume both cleanups above rather than leaving them to be rediscovered.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the existing manifest-sync hook is the closest precedent for shape and failure mode.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **ci check for drift between mcp server tool lists and agent frontmatter tools: entries** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session finding, 2026-08-22\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"723e41c188c7a31a148316d10ca803d4cc2fdfab6e01ad6fc9e928bb46221914\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQLLlTw\"}"}